            'description' => 'A customer guide to deposits, progress payments, financing, receipts, balances, credits, and fraud prevention.',
            'content' => '<div class="sc-cover"><span class="sc-kicker">Smart Choice Customer Guide</span><h2>Managing Payments and Financial Records Safely</h2><p>A customer guide to deposits, progress payments, financing, receipts, balances, credits, and fraud prevention.</p><blockquote>Professional information designed to help you make confident decisions before, during, and after your project.</blockquote></div><div class="sc-grid"><div class="sc-card"><h3>What this guide covers</h3><p>Planning, responsibilities, communication, documentation, safety, and the practical steps that support a successful customer experience.</p></div><div class="sc-card"><h3>How to use it</h3><p>Read the complete guide, keep it with your project records, and return to the relevant section whenever a decision or question arises.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">1</span><div><h3>Understand the Payment Schedule</h3><p>The contract or approved document identifies when payments are due. Common milestones include deposit, material ordering, mobilization, progress stages, inspection stages, substantial completion, and final closeout. Payment timing should be reviewed before work begins so funds are available when required.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">2</span><div><h3>Invoices and Balances</h3><p>Each invoice should identify the project, amount, due date, line items, credits, and prior payments. The account balance may include more than one invoice or approved change. Contact accounting promptly when a payment appears missing or applied incorrectly.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">3</span><div><h3>Financing</h3><p>Financing programs are governed by the lender or provider, which may have separate disclosures, approval requirements, payment terms, interest, promotional conditions, and funding procedures. Approval for financing does not automatically modify the construction agreement unless the change is documented.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">4</span><div><h3>Receipts and Proof of Payment</h3><p>Keep receipts, transaction confirmations, canceled checks, and financing records. When paying electronically, verify the company name, invoice number, amount, and destination. A verbal statement that payment was made is not a substitute for a traceable record.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">5</span><div><h3>Credits, Refunds, and Adjustments</h3><p>Credits or refunds may require review of completed work, ordered materials, restocking charges, nonrefundable items, financing transactions, or contract terms. Adjustments should appear in the account record or written agreement. Allow reasonable processing time after approval.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">6</span><div><h3>Fraud Prevention</h3><p>Be cautious with unexpected payment instructions, changed bank details, urgent wire requests, or messages from unfamiliar addresses. Verify changes through a known company contact before sending funds. Never provide passwords or complete card information through an ordinary support message.</p></div></div><h2>Customer Action Checklist</h2><ul class="sc-checklist"><li>Read all project documents and attachments before approval.</li><li>Keep contact information and authorized decision-makers current.</li><li>Use the client portal and support tickets for tracked communication.</li><li>Respond promptly to selections, access requests, and approvals.</li><li>Keep copies of signed documents, payments, receipts, and closeout records.</li><li>Report safety concerns or unexpected conditions as soon as they are discovered.</li></ul><div class="sc-success"><strong>Smart Choice Standard:</strong> Done Right Through Professional Service. Our objective is to combine skilled construction coordination with clear records, respectful communication, and dependable customer support.</div>',
