        $guides[] = [
            'name' => 'Safety During Construction',
            'slug' => 'smart-choice-customer-safety',
            'title' => 'Customer Safety During Active Construction',
            'description' => 'Important rules for work zones, tools, utilities, temporary conditions, children, pets, and emergency situations.',
            'content' => '<div class="sc-cover"><span class="sc-kicker">Smart Choice Customer Guide</span><h2>Customer Safety During Active Construction</h2><p>Important rules for work zones, tools, utilities, temporary conditions, children, pets, and emergency situations.</p><blockquote>Professional information designed to help you make confident decisions before, during, and after your project.</blockquote></div><div class="sc-grid"><div class="sc-card"><h3>What this guide covers</h3><p>Planning, responsibilities, communication, documentation, safety, and the practical steps that support a successful customer experience.</p></div><div class="sc-card"><h3>How to use it</h3><p>Read the complete guide, keep it with your project records, and return to the relevant section whenever a decision or question arises.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">1</span><div><h3>Respect Work-Zone Boundaries</h3><p>Active work areas may contain open walls, exposed wiring, unfinished floors, ladders, sharp materials, power tools, temporary supports, and debris. Do not enter restricted zones without permission. Barriers and warning signs must remain in place until the responsible trade removes them.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">2</span><div><h3>Children and Pets</h3><p>Children and pets should never be allowed to roam through a construction area. Noise, open doors, unfamiliar workers, and equipment can create unexpected behavior. Arrange secure supervision before the crew arrives.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">3</span><div><h3>Utilities</h3><p>Do not operate disconnected fixtures, energize open circuits, restore shutoff valves, or use equipment marked out of service. Temporary interruptions may be required for testing and safe installation. Ask the project contact before using a system that is under construction.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">4</span><div><h3>Dust and Air Quality</h3><p>Demolition and cutting can produce dust and odors. Keep sensitive occupants away from active work, follow recommendations for ventilation, and notify the team of known health sensitivities before the work begins. Do not remove containment because it appears inconvenient.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">5</span><div><h3>Emergency Conditions</h3><p>For fire, gas odor, electrical arcing, active flooding, structural movement, or immediate danger, leave the affected area and contact the appropriate emergency service or utility. The customer portal is not an emergency response system. Document the event with Smart Choice after immediate safety is addressed.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">6</span><div><h3>Daily Awareness</h3><p>Wear appropriate footwear near work areas, avoid touching tools or materials, keep access routes clear, and follow instructions from the site supervisor. Safety is a shared responsibility and takes priority over convenience or schedule.</p></div></div><h2>Customer Action Checklist</h2><ul class="sc-checklist"><li>Read all project documents and attachments before approval.</li><li>Keep contact information and authorized decision-makers current.</li><li>Use the client portal and support tickets for tracked communication.</li><li>Respond promptly to selections, access requests, and approvals.</li><li>Keep copies of signed documents, payments, receipts, and closeout records.</li><li>Report safety concerns or unexpected conditions as soon as they are discovered.</li></ul><div class="sc-success"><strong>Smart Choice Standard:</strong> Done Right Through Professional Service. Our objective is to combine skilled construction coordination with clear records, respectful communication, and dependable customer support.</div>',
