            'slug' => 'smart-choice-maintenance-guide',
            'title' => 'Protecting Your Improvement After Project Completion',
            'description' => 'How to maintain finishes, monitor sealants and moisture, use products correctly, and preserve project records.',
            'content' => '<div class="sc-cover"><span class="sc-kicker">Smart Choice Customer Guide</span><h2>Protecting Your Improvement After Project Completion</h2><p>How to maintain finishes, monitor sealants and moisture, use products correctly, and preserve project records.</p><blockquote>Professional information designed to help you make confident decisions before, during, and after your project.</blockquote></div><div class="sc-grid"><div class="sc-card"><h3>What this guide covers</h3><p>Planning, responsibilities, communication, documentation, safety, and the practical steps that support a successful customer experience.</p></div><div class="sc-card"><h3>How to use it</h3><p>Read the complete guide, keep it with your project records, and return to the relevant section whenever a decision or question arises.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">1</span><div><h3>Follow Manufacturer Instructions</h3><p>Products such as flooring, countertops, cabinets, windows, fixtures, coatings, appliances, sealants, and waterproofing systems have specific cleaning and maintenance requirements. Use approved products and avoid harsh chemicals or abrasive tools that can damage the finish.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">2</span><div><h3>Moisture Management</h3><p>Water intrusion and uncontrolled humidity can damage many building materials. Maintain caulking, grout, drainage, gutters, exterior sealants, and ventilation. Report leaks promptly and do not allow standing water to remain against walls, floors, cabinets, or exterior openings.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">3</span><div><h3>Normal Movement and Wear</h3><p>Buildings expand, contract, settle, and respond to temperature and humidity. Minor cosmetic movement can occur at joints and transitions. High-impact use, furniture movement, pets, sunlight, and cleaning methods also affect wear. Routine maintenance preserves appearance and performance.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">4</span><div><h3>Mechanical and Electrical Systems</h3><p>Replace filters, keep equipment clear, test safety devices, and follow service schedules. Do not alter wiring, plumbing, HVAC, or controls without qualified assistance. Unauthorized modifications can create hazards and complicate future service.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">5</span><div><h3>Documentation</h3><p>Keep product names, model numbers, colors, leftover materials, receipts, warranties, photographs, and final documents. These records are valuable for maintenance, replacement parts, insurance, resale, and future renovations.</p></div></div><div class="sc-step"><span class="sc-step-number">6</span><div><h3>When to Request Service</h3><p>Report unusual leaks, movement, odors, noises, electrical behavior, or performance problems early. Provide photographs and a clear description through the support system. Prompt reporting can limit damage and help determine whether the condition relates to installation, maintenance, product performance, or another cause.</p></div></div><h2>Customer Action Checklist</h2><ul class="sc-checklist"><li>Read all project documents and attachments before approval.</li><li>Keep contact information and authorized decision-makers current.</li><li>Use the client portal and support tickets for tracked communication.</li><li>Respond promptly to selections, access requests, and approvals.</li><li>Keep copies of signed documents, payments, receipts, and closeout records.</li><li>Report safety concerns or unexpected conditions as soon as they are discovered.</li></ul><div class="sc-success"><strong>Smart Choice Standard:</strong> Done Right Through Professional Service. Our objective is to combine skilled construction coordination with clear records, respectful communication, and dependable customer support.</div>',
